## What and why

- Three gaps a real suite hit on its first day. Each is small on its own; together they are what stopped a one-file iteration loop from working. The fourth, templating run-unique params in the trace cache, is split out into its own PR so this one is easier to land.
- **Single-file runs pull in their setup.** `e2e run login.e2e.ts` failed with `COLLECTION_ERROR` when the session it consumes is produced by `auth.setup.e2e.ts`, which the docs said would work. Collection now imports every discovered file and stamps `selected` on files and tests from the positionals: unselected ordinary tests are report-only unselected results (as tag-filtered tests already are), a consumed session promotes its setup wherever it lives, and focus (`.only`) is decided among selected tests only. A collection error in any file now fails a single-file run too, as it does for a runner that loads the suite whole.
- **Runtime skip.** `test.skip(condition, reason)` inside a body skips the running test for a fact only the app can tell (one organization, a flag that is off). Steps that ran stay in the report, teardown runs, no retry is spent, the suite realm survives, a serial member that skips stays skipped, a setup test cannot skip (`INVALID_ARGUMENT`), and the call outside a body is `COLLECTION_ERROR`. The whole API lives in `internal/skip.ts`; the signal is recognized by brand, not `instanceof`, because the test module realm may resolve `e2e` to another copy of the package. `records.ts` now owns `AttemptStatus` and `isFailedStatus`, the one question the runner asks of a verdict. Wire change: a skipped attempt may carry steps and a `skip` reason.
- **Matchers people reach for.** `expect(actual, message)` opens a value failure with the caller's label, so a report never says a bare `expected false to be true`. `toBeGreaterThanOrEqual`, `toBeLessThanOrEqual`, `toBeCloseTo` join the value matchers and `expect.poll`. `getByRole({ level })` came in through #324 and is used as-is here.
```ts
test('switches organizations', { session: 'admin' }, async ({ app, agent, api }) => {
  const organizations = await api.list('/api/directory/organizations');
  test.skip(organizations.length < 2, 'the demo tenant has a single organization');
  await app.open('/backend');
  await agent.act(`switch to "${organizations[1].name}"`);
});
```

Key seams: `packages/e2e/src/collect/collect.ts` (`selected`), `packages/e2e/src/collect/select.ts`, `packages/e2e/src/internal/skip.ts` + `run/execute.ts` (`emitUnitResult`), `packages/e2e/src/run/records.ts` (`AttemptStatus`, `isFailedStatus`), `packages/e2e/src/expect/values.ts`.

