## What and why

- Split out of #325 (now merged) and rebased onto `main`.
- Every `act` with `{ params: { name: unique } }` missed the trace cache on every run: the key digested the value, and the recording carried it in typed text, the tapped option's name, and the end anchors. On the suite this came from: 23 misses, 4 replays, with nothing changed.
- `unique(value)` marks such a param. It rides the same projection walk as `Secret`: the model and the executor see the plain string, and the walk lists the marked leaves by JSON Pointer. The key digests the params with `{{param:/pointer}}` where the value was, the recording carries the same placeholder wherever its text spelled the value (inputs, target text, anchors, summaries, paths), and replay fills it from the current call. Unmarked params stay literal.
- No heuristic and nothing to pin: the first draft templated every string of three or more characters and needed a `literalParams` field in trace-1 to stay safe when a param steered the flow without appearing in text. With an explicit marker that mechanism, the threshold, and the trace-format change are gone; `identity.ts` and the key builder are unchanged.
- `trace.ts` owns `mapTraceText`, the one list of text-bearing trace fields; `template.ts` is the placeholder grammar plus the key-side and trace-side substitutions; `params.ts` is the marker.

```ts
import { unique } from 'e2e';

const name = `E2E ${Date.now()} Company`;
await agent.act('Create a new company named {name}', { params: { name: unique(name) } });
// key: { name: '{{param:/name}}' }
// recording: type {{param:/name}} into textbox Name; tap option {{param:/name}}
```

Fail-closed: a placeholder the current call did not mark is a miss, and a recording whose text already spelled a placeholder is not written.

## Checklist

- [x] Changeset added (`pnpm changeset`) for any change to a published package, or the change is testbed, docs, or CI only.
- [ ] Breaking change: title carries `!`, the changeset body names what breaks and what replaces it, and the deprecation warning landed a window earlier (stability policy in CONTRIBUTING.md).
