Three artifact kinds carried a registered secret under a clean label. A download was recorded `redaction: 'complete'` without anyone reading it, so an exported CSV holding a configured API key reached the report and the `ArtifactStore` as fully masked. A trace was rewritten only after a secret fill, although a settings page can render a configured value with no fill at all and the engine sends `web({ headers })` on every request the trace records. A restored session re-sent its cookies on every request, and `redactTraceArchives` knew nothing about them.

- Downloads are scanned when the attempt settles, against the ledger as it stands then, so a value a provider resolves after the file was written counts (`packages/e2e/src/run/artifacts.ts`). One that holds a value is deleted, recorded as `incomplete` with no `path`, `size`, or `sha256`, kept from the store, and explained with `ARTIFACT_WITHHELD` in the attempt's `secondaryErrors`, attributed to the phase that produced the file rather than the one running when the scan ran. Without a store the file is streamed through `SecretLedger.byteScanner`, so a large export never sits whole in the worker. Every sink has a ledger: the `e2e mcp` live session and a serial group hand over their session's.
- The trace decision no longer reads the pixel taint. `closeSession` rewrites every archive whenever the session ledger holds a value and labels the result `complete`; `not-required` now means the ledger was empty (`packages/e2e/src/run/execute.ts:615`). `redactTraceArchives` already rewrites only an archive something changed in.
- `EngineAttemptContext.registerSecret(name, value)` is an engine's way into the ledger (`packages/e2e/src/engine/index.ts:522`). The harness binds it to the session ledger and `processSecrets` and restricts the name to the alphabet secret names share (`packages/e2e/src/run/secrecy.ts:39`).
- The member is harness-provided: engines consume the context in `startAttempt`, they do not implement it, so a third-party engine built on spi 1 keeps working unchanged and can ignore the member. Only test doubles that construct the context by hand had to add it. Per the engine-contract rule in `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `@e2edev/mobile` gets a changeset too, although its code did not change: it registers nothing through the member yet. The other way round, a newer `@e2edev/web` on an `e2e` that predates the member, is admitted by the peer range; the engine then refuses to start the attempt with `ENGINE_FAILURE` naming the update when it holds a header, basic-auth password, or restored value to register, and runs as before when it holds none.
- The web engine registers each `headers` value of 16 characters or more as `header.<name>` and the `basicAuth` password at `startAttempt` (`packages/web/src/surface.ts:365`), and each cookie and local-storage value of 16 characters or more as `cookie.<name>` and `storage.<key>` on `captureState` and `restoreState` (`packages/web/src/session-secrets.ts:20`). A registered value is rewritten out of model input too, so the floor keeps a `theme=dark` cookie or an `accept-language: en` header from mangling every screen that contains the word. IndexedDB records are not walked.
- `docs/security.mdx` gains a downloads row, its trace and headers bullets say what is now true, and the sessions section names the length floor and IndexedDB as the remaining exceptions. `ARTIFACT_WITHHELD` joins `reference/errors.mdx`; the engine reference lists the new member.

| Artifact | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- |
| download, clean | `complete`, unread | `complete`, scanned at settle |
| download holding a registered value | `complete`, raw bytes stored | deleted, `incomplete`, no path, `ARTIFACT_WITHHELD` |
| trace after a secret fill | rewritten, `complete` | rewritten, `complete` |
| trace of a page rendering a static secret, or with `headers`, no fill | raw, `not-required` | rewritten, `complete` |
| trace of a restored session | raw `cookie` header, `not-required` | `<secret:cookie.<name>>`, `complete` |
| trace with an empty ledger | raw, `not-required` | raw, `not-required` |

