- Fix in `packages/e2e/src/run/artifacts.ts`: any value the safe alphabet rewrote (or that is only dots, or is past the cap) now ends in an 8-hex digest of the whole original, the same shape a cut long id already had. A value that was already safe within the cap is unchanged, so those directories stay where they were.
- Chose the digest suffix over an escaping scheme (`_xx` per unsafe byte) because a test id nearly always carries `/` and `::`; escaping would turn `tests/auth.e2e.ts::auth::signs in` into `tests_2fauth.e2e.ts_3a_3aauth_3a_3asigns_20in`, while the digest keeps `tests_auth.e2e.ts__auth__signs_in-1a2b3c4d`.
- Every directory name of an ordinary test id moves once (gains the suffix). Report paths in `report.json` come from the same segments, so they match what lands on disk; the markdown reporter's `failures/<page>.md` name gains the suffix too. Nothing in `docs/` or `packages/github` describes the segment shape.

```ts
export function sanitizePathSegment(value: string): string {
  const sanitized = /^\.+$/.test(value) ? '_' : value.replaceAll(/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/g, '_');
  if (sanitized === value && sanitized.length <= MAX_SEGMENT_CHARS) return sanitized;
  const digest = createHash('sha256').update(value).digest('hex').slice(0, SEGMENT_DIGEST_CHARS);
  return `${sanitized.slice(0, MAX_SEGMENT_CHARS - SEGMENT_DIGEST_CHARS - 1)}-${digest}`;
}
```

