## Summary

With `@e2e-dev/web`, `screen.getByRole(role, name)` fails with `InvalidSelectorError` as soon as the
string `name` contains a straight apostrophe (`'`, U+0027). The same element is found with a regular
expression in which the apostrophe is written `\x27`, so the element and the name are fine: the
selector built by the engine is not parseable.

