### What happened

With two iOS simulators booted, `video: 'on'`, and the target's `device` pinned to one of them by UDID, a test that starts after the previous one ended its session fails before its body runs:

```
ENGINE_FAILURE: start video recording failed: 2 devices match this request equally; select one explicitly.
```

Expected: the attempt records the pinned simulator, as every other device command targets it. With a single simulator booted the same suite passes.

In a real suite this cascades: one test failed on a covered tap, and every test after it failed with this error, 1 real failure turning into 6.

`startVideo` is the only device command that does not pass the worker's selection: https://github.com/tester-army/e2e/blob/b7ba0097/packages/mobile/src/surface.ts#L577-L589. `boot`, `open`, and `install` spread `this.selection()`. While the session has an app open, agent-device resolves the device from it; after `closeApp()` (or a failed attempt) the session names none, and the device-scope start is ambiguous.

