## What and why

`scripts/check-docs-examples.ts` guards one invariant: every file under `docs/examples/` is shown verbatim on a docs page or in `skills/e2e/`, so the copy on a page cannot drift from the file it came from. It only guarded half of it. The check walked a hand-kept `EXAMPLES` map of file to page, which caught a page drifting from its example but never noticed an example that no page showed at all: the file was not a key in the map, so nothing read it and the script passed. `AGENTS.md` states the invariant as "`docs/examples/` is typechecked and shown verbatim on docs pages and in `skills/e2e/`", and nothing else enforces it. `tsc` typechecks an example whether or not a page shows it, so an unshown example could land and stay.

This is the same shape as the hand-kept list `scripts/check-error-codes.ts` used to carry for its source roots. There the literal array had already drifted: `packages/eas/src` and `packages/smol/src` raised codes the reference was supposed to document, and neither was ever scanned, so the check stayed green while the reference went stale. This map has not drifted yet, since every example added so far also edited it, but it is the same manual step, and the open engine pull requests each add their new example to it by hand. One forgotten line and the check is silent again.

The fix reads the file list from the filesystem and reports any example the map does not carry. The map stays, because it is the only place that knows which page shows an example; the filesystem decides whether an example exists at all. That is the split `error-codes.ts` already uses, deriving the roots and leaving the checker to read them.

```ts
// scripts/docs-examples.ts
export function exampleFiles(): string[] {
  const files: string[] = [];
  const walk = (dir: string): void => {
    for (const entry of readdirSync(join(REPO_ROOT, dir), { withFileTypes: true })) {
      const path = `${dir}/${entry.name}`;
      if (entry.isDirectory()) walk(path);
      else if (entry.name.endsWith('.ts')) files.push(path);
    }
  };
  walk('docs/examples');
  return files.toSorted();
}

export function unmappedExamples(mapped: Iterable<string>): string[] {
  const known = new Set(mapped);
  return exampleFiles().filter((file) => !known.has(file));
}
```

`check-docs-examples.ts` reports a forgotten file before it checks the mapped ones, so one run lists both a drifted page and an unshown example:

```text
docs/examples/web/orphan-example.ts: no page shows this example; add it to EXAMPLES and to the page that should
docs/browser.mdx: no code block matches docs/examples/web/browser-provider.ts
```

`scripts/docs-examples.test.ts` covers the walk, an empty map, a complete map, and the forgotten file. `scripts/docs-examples.ts` holds the two functions on their own so the test imports them without the checker's `main()` running, the same `install-scripts.ts` / `check-install-scripts.ts` split already in `scripts/`.

No changeset: this is a repo-side check under `scripts/`, not a published package.

| | main | this branch |
| --- | --- | --- |
| examples the check reads | the 14 keys in the map | every `.ts` under `docs/examples/` |
| an example added with no page | silently passes, exit 0 | fails, exit 1 |
| a page drifting from its example | fails, exit 1 | fails, exit 1 |
| `scripts/**/*.test.ts` | 17 pass | 22 pass |

A note for the reviewer: a few open pull requests add a new engine's example to this map by hand. This change does not conflict with them, and it does not remove the line they add. It only makes forgetting that line fail the check instead of passing quietly.

