## Restoration check

Follow the revised auth doctor on the same healthy fixture. It must execute the setup and a check of restored signed-in state, with an observable passing result. Then make the setup fail before saving its session and confirm the doctor reports that failure. A command that merely collects tests or suppresses `NO_TESTS` does not restore the auth-check contract. The generator and its reference example must agree.

## Suggested wording

Describe an auth doctor as an ordinary signed-in smoke test that consumes a named session. Selecting that test runs its setup and checks the restored state. Do not present the setup-only command as a runnable auth doctor or as a way to persist sessions for later runs.

