- The skill and the docs said "one goal per `act`" but never said what a goal is, and their own examples broke the rule: `'add a todo named "Buy milk" and mark it done'`, `'add todos ..., complete the first'`.
- An atomic goal is now defined as one outcome that one check confirms. Two parts that each leave a state worth checking are two goals, each with its own `act` and check. Steps toward one outcome (opening the screen that holds a control, scrolling, closing a banner, filling one form) are the path and stay with the agent.
- `docs/core-concepts.mdx#goals` owns the rule and shows a titled Bad and Good block. `agent-steps`, `quickstart`, `ci`, and `coding-agents` link to it instead of restating it.
- `skills/e2e/references/agent.md` carries the same rule with `// BAD:` and `// GOOD:` comments, since skills render no titles; `SKILL.md` Rules has the short version.

```ts
// BAD: three goals in one instruction, one recording, no check between them.
await agent.act('open the Pro plan, set the seats to {seats}, and check out', { params: { seats: 3 } });

// GOOD: three atomic goals, each pinned before the next.
await agent.act('open the Pro plan');
await expect(screen.getByRole('heading', 'Pro plan')).toBeVisible();
await agent.act('set the seats to {seats}', { params: { seats: 3 } });
await expect(screen.getByRole('status', 'Seats')).toHaveText('3 seats');
await agent.act('check out');
await expect(screen.getByText('Order confirmed')).toBeVisible();
```

Examples split into one `act` per goal, each followed by a check: core-concepts' opening test, the Cypress migration, coding-agents' cart test, and the skill's "Buy milk" act. The decision-models example drops ", and verify it is listed" from its instruction; the `expect` and `agent.assert` after it already do that.

Left as they are, on purpose:
- `tools.mdx` `'seed the cart with SKU {sku}, then check out'`: seeding is a runner-side API call the page does not show, so it is a path step toward checkout. It gains the missing check on `Order confirmed`.
- `mobile.mdx` `'go to General, then About'`, `reference/runner.mdx` `'open settings and turn on dark mode'`: navigation toward one outcome, which the path list now names.
- The benchmark agentic suites keep their compound scenario goals; splitting them re-records the committed cache.

