### Problem

The model is fixed in the committed `e2e.config.ts`, but which key is available differs per machine. One teammate has an Anthropic key, another an AI Gateway key, and switching means editing the config.

We build [cezar](https://github.com/open-mercato/cezar), a local orchestrator that runs coding-agent tasks in parallel git worktrees and gates each task on check steps. e2e is the browser check we recommend; cezar sets it up for users in one click (it runs `e2e init`, configures the project, and proves it with `e2e list` and `e2e run`).

cezar stores each user's model key encrypted and hands it only to check steps. The key is per user while the config is per repo.

