### What happened

After text entry, a deterministic tap can use bounds captured before the keyboard moves the form. In an iOS simulator recording, a password-visibility control was resolved at y=298; the keyboard then moved it to about y=211, but the tap landed at y=298. The subsequent assertion failed.

Expected: after text entry, honor the remaining configured transition budget and resolve the next control again before dispatch.

The mobile engine records the pre-entry index after type/fill/clear. settled() skips its transition wait when the first post-entry snapshot has the same bounds. That snapshot can precede keyboard movement, so an unchanged first frame is not sufficient.

Separately, agent-device can refuse a moving target with reason=target_still_moving and dispatched=no. The engine currently classifies that as nonretryable ENGINE_FAILURE, even though re-observing is safe when no input was dispatched. Unknown dispatch status must remain nonretryable.

