### What happened

A replayed `agent.act` step whose last action starts a navigation hands off with `end-mismatch` (`REPLAY_STALE` under `--strict-cache`) when the destination commits more than about 5 s after the action, even though `END_PATH_TIMEOUT_MS` is 15 s.

`StepTraceSession.endScreen` (`packages/e2e/src/agent/step-cache.ts`) takes `END_PATH_DELAYS_MS[attempt]` and returns once that is `undefined`. The list `[100, 300, 600, 1000, 3000]` adds up to 5 s, so the loop stops there and the 15 s bound is never reached. `pollSettled` in `replay.ts` already repeats its last delay until its timeout.

Code: [`step-cache.ts` L146-147](https://github.com/tester-army/e2e/blob/69e123b17e04ed624df16d32f3b1ef95ce22c083/packages/e2e/src/agent/step-cache.ts#L146-L147), [L530](https://github.com/tester-army/e2e/blob/69e123b17e04ed624df16d32f3b1ef95ce22c083/packages/e2e/src/agent/step-cache.ts#L530), [`replay.ts` L613](https://github.com/tester-army/e2e/blob/69e123b17e04ed624df16d32f3b1ef95ce22c083/packages/e2e/src/agent/replay.ts#L613).

Expected, as PR #126 (which added this wait) describes it ("polls the path with the same settling backoff anchors use (100..3000 ms, 15 s cap, bounded by the step budget and the abort signal)"): keep polling at 3 s until 15 s. Seen: hand-off at 5.0 s. This is only about reaching the 15 s already chosen, not about whether 15 s is the right bound (#1144).

