### What happened

A step whose end state shows an alert with an ISO timestamp (`Saved at 2026-10-24T15:41:27.955Z`) records, then can fail its replay when the new timestamp differs: in the minutes or seconds of a whole-second instant (`…:30:00Z`), in the milliseconds of a fractional one (`…:30:00.120Z`). It fails with `REPLAY_STALE (end-mismatch)` under `--strict-cache`, a hand-off otherwise. The detail names the recorded alert as missing and the new one as unrecorded.

`docs/cache.mdx` says volatile text in an alert "reads as a placeholder", and it does for `17:42` or `2026-10-22`. For an instant, the id pattern in `VOLATILE_TEXT` (`cache/anchors.ts`) takes only `2026-10-22T09`. The clock pattern then misses `30:00Z` (it needs a word boundary, and `Z` follows) and leaves `.120Z` of a fractional one, so most pairs of saves compare unequal.

Code: [`VOLATILE_TEXT`](https://github.com/tester-army/e2e/blob/69e123b17e04ed624df16d32f3b1ef95ce22c083/packages/e2e/src/cache/anchors.ts#L149), [`alertShape`](https://github.com/tester-army/e2e/blob/69e123b17e04ed624df16d32f3b1ef95ce22c083/packages/e2e/src/cache/anchors.ts#L211-L212).

