### What happened

The mobile engine omits the selected simulator ID from snapshots, so reads fail with `AMBIGUOUS_MATCH` after the app connection is lost. This occurs with two booted simulators.

The `device` option contains an explicit simulator ID. The initial `boot` request includes it as `udid`, but `snapshot` omits it.

Expected: every command uses the selected simulator.

Actual: a snapshot falls back to automatic device selection after the app connection closes or is lost.

### Minimal reproduction

This test uses an HTTP fixture for the closed app. It needs no simulator or model. The final assertion fails on `@e2e-dev/mobile` 0.12.4.

