expect.toHaveCount passed :: getByRole("row", name: "Record B")
```

The report calls the old text a `recorded verdict`. The next step only sees `observed` and cannot see that the summary describes another run.

In a real model-backed run, the agent failed a step because it saw two different names. The small example below only captures the conflicting input. It does not depend on a model making the same mistake.

**Expected:** The next agent step needs a clear way to tell an old summary from a current result.

I am not asking to replace names inside old model text. #558 explains why that can change the meaning of a summary.

