### What happened

Replay deletes the correct row, but an unrelated clock value makes the replay fail its end check.

The requested task is to delete `Example record`. The clock is not part of that task.

| Run | Clock before → after Delete | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Record | `10:00` → `09:59` | Pass, recording saved |
| Replay | `20:00` → `19:59` | `REPLAY_STALE (end-mismatch)` |
| Control replay | `20:00` → `09:59` | Pass, full replay |

All three runs delete the same row. The failed replay completes 1/1 actions, then reports:

```text
every recorded action ran, but the recorded end state did not show on /: missing node "09:59"
```

Without `--strict-cache`, this end check hands the step to the agent instead of failing the run directly.

**Expected:** The clock value is not a required result of this delete task. A different time must not be the only reason to reject this replay. Missing task results and new error messages must still stop replay.

