## What and why

- A custom tool can't call agent-device today. `getToolContext()` only has `observe` and `attachScreenshot`, and a client built by hand misses the engine's daemon, lease, and per-worker session. So agent-device features with no e2e tool (mobile data, simulated phone calls, Bluetooth, hardware buttons) are out of the agent's reach without a fork.
- `deviceSession(...engines)` on `@e2e-dev/mobile/tools` returns the running attempt's `DeviceSession`, the same object a test gets from `device.unstable_raw`. It reuses the running-attempt lookup `mobileTools` already had, which is now shared.
- `@e2e-dev/mobile/agent-device` re-exports agent-device's types and error helpers, so the tool needs no `agent-device` dependency of its own. It has no client factory.
- Both are unstable, like `unstable_raw`. The main entry and the `agent-device` pin don't change.

