### Summary
When running mobile tests against a real iOS device on BrowserStack App Automate, the test assertions execute and pass, but the run fails during engine teardown with `ENGINE_FAILURE (cleanup)`.

Inspecting the raw BrowserStack Appium logs shows that `agent-device` never sends `DELETE /session/:sessionId` when finishing the target. As a result, the BrowserStack session remains open until BrowserStack's 90-second idle timeout terminates it (`BROWSERSTACK_IDLE_TIMEOUT`), blocking parallel session slots in the meantime.

