Inside a test body, `test.skip(condition, reason)` and `test.fail(condition, reason)` treat every condition that is not a boolean as true. Playwright reads the condition by truthiness.

Repro (testbed, built CLI on `main`):

```ts
test('only on CI', async () => {
  test.skip(process.env.CI, 'flaky on CI'); // CI unset: e2e skips, Playwright runs the test
});

test('known gap on CI', async () => {
  test.fail(process.env.CI, 'known CI gap'); // CI unset: the passing test fails with UNEXPECTED_PASS
});
```

- `undefined`, `null`, `0`, and `''` as the condition all skip or mark the test.
- `parseModifierCall` in `packages/e2e/src/internal/skip.ts` keeps a condition only when it is a boolean, so any other value counts as `true`.
- A Promise (a condition missing its `await`) or a function as the condition also always skips or marks the test. `test.skipIf` already refuses a Promise.

