### What happened

On a device target, `check()` and `uncheck()` tap the control once and return. They never read its state again. So `uncheck()` on a checked radio resolves while the radio stays checked, and a toggle that ignores the tap passes `check()` too. The web engine reads the state after the click until the deadline. When it doesn't change, the web engine fails with `NOT_ACTIONABLE`. It also refuses `uncheck()` on a radio ("uncheck cannot clear a radio button; select another radio in its group", `packages/web/src/actions.ts`). The mobile engine (`packages/mobile/src/surface.ts`, `case 'check' / 'uncheck'`) does neither.

### Reproduction

https://github.com/e2e-inc/e2e/tree/3e7d19d/apps/mobile-benchmark (Control Inventory scenario, Toggles tab)

### Steps to reproduce

1. Build and install the mobile benchmark on an iOS simulator.
2. Run this test against the `ios-simulator` target:
   ```ts
   test('uncheck on a checked radio', async ({ app, device, screen }) => {
     await openScenario({ app, device, screen }, 'Control Inventory');
     await screen.getByTestId('tab-toggles').tap();
     const small = screen.getByRole('radio', 'Small');
     await expect(small).toBeChecked();
     await small.uncheck();
     await expect(small).not.toBeChecked();
   });
   ```
3. `uncheck()` passes (`✓ locator.uncheck getByRole("radio", name: "Small")`, 1.9 s). The radio stays checked and `size-status` still reads `size: Small`. The test fails only at the next `expect`, which points at the wrong line.

Expected: `uncheck()` fails with `NOT_ACTIONABLE`, as on the web.

### Versions

e2e 0.24.0, @e2e-dev/mobile 0.12.8 (main at 3e7d19d), agent-device 0.21.40, Node 24.22.3, iPhone 17 Pro simulator on iOS 26.5

